# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the Sanitizer Tests workflow
# (.github/workflows/sanitizers.yml loads this file through UBSAN_OPTIONS).
#
# Only defects inside third-party or ecosystem code belong here, each with the
# upstream issue and the condition for removing it. Never suppress
# pacs_system code: a pacs_system test that fails under a sanitizer is
# quarantined in ctest-quarantine-<sanitizer>.txt with its issue instead.
# A pattern matches the source file of the report as a substring.

# OpenJPH 0.21.5 (FetchContent pin in cmake/dependencies.cmake):
# mem_elastic_allocator::get_buffer() advances its store by
# needed_bytes + sizeof(coded_lists) without rounding, so each coded_lists
# after the first is constructed at an arbitrary byte offset
# (others/ojph_mem.cpp:91-118). The constructor and every later access through
# such an object are misaligned; the files below are where those accesses
# are reported. Only the alignment check is suppressed, and only in these
# OpenJPH files. Fixed upstream by aous72/OpenJPH#262 (commit 0ec2184, first
# released in 0.27.0); remove these entries when the OpenJPH pin is 0.27.0
# or later.
alignment:openjph-src/src/core/others/ojph_mem.cpp
alignment:openjph-src/src/core/common/ojph_mem.h
alignment:openjph-src/src/core/coding/ojph_block_encoder
alignment:openjph-src/src/core/codestream/ojph_bitbuffer_read.h
alignment:openjph-src/src/core/codestream/ojph_bitbuffer_write.h
alignment:openjph-src/src/core/codestream/ojph_codeblock.cpp
alignment:openjph-src/src/core/codestream/ojph_precinct.cpp
